{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nOutside the agent sandbox on 2026-11-20 at about 06:00 PST (host load average 25-45 from concurrent verifies), `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle` failed 2 of 2 serial runs with `concurrent.futures.TimeoutError` from `future.result(timeout=60)` (test line 401), after 247 s and 203 s of wall time.\n\n## Root cause (verified): two fixed wall-clock bounds\n1. The test's own `future.result(timeout=60)` per worker. Removed by e7532d2b71c (Gerrit 3480, allstar-sleepy-armadillo), which joins plain processes without a per-worker bound.\n2. Still live after that rewrite: `_merge_ref` in `src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py` takes the store write lock with `timeout=10, attempts=1` and no retries, unlike every canonical store write (`write_path_retries()`, default 30 s windows with 2 retry passes). When both workers close the same ticket, the one that waits gives up after a single 10 s window whenever the other holds the lock longer, which a slow host produces, and its close fails with `completion candidate merge failed: flock: could not acquire lock after 10s`. A real concurrent close on a loaded host fails the same way.\n\nDeterministic reproduction (Nov 20 2026, PATH `git` shim sleeping a fixed delay before every git start, `-o timeout=2000` so only the bounds under test can fire):\n- Before e7532d2b71c (worktree at e7532d2b71c^): `TimeoutError` at delays of 1.5 s, 2.5 s and 4 s (1 failed each).\n- At origin/main (after e7532d2b71c): `AssertionError: a commit worker raised: CommandError('Error: completion candidate merge failed: flock: could not acquire lock after 10s ...')` at 1.5 s, 2.5 s and 4 s.\n- With the change below, at 1.5 s: 1 passed (call 181.69 s).\n\n## Approach\nIn `_merge_ref`, take the lock with the canonical write-path budget, `store_lock.write_lock(tracker, dual_window=True, retries=store_lock.write_path_retries())`, the same call `event_append` uses for every store write. The merge itself is unchanged and stays under the lock; only how long a waiter waits changes. No config key, environment variable or flag is added (`write_path_retries()` is the existing resolver).\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py`\n\n## Testing\n- The 1.5 s shim run of the race test: fails before (lock timeout) and passes after, both recorded on this ticket.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py` and the completion-delivery unit tests pass without a shim.\n- `make verify` through the verify slot.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic reproduction is recorded here, for both the original 60 s bound and the remaining 10 s merge-lock bound.\n- [ ] Under the 1.5 s-per-start shim the race test passes with the change, and fails without it, runs recorded here.\n- [ ] The completion candidate merge waits on the canonical write-path lock budget.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes and Gerrit gives Verified +1.","title":"Concurrent close of one ticket fails on a slow host: completion merge waits a single 10 s lock window (and the test once waited 60 s per worker)"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795244685247323001,"uuid":"902da330-d08e-4580-aca9-50d55ba2f271"}